[BLAME] benchmark_3/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: DAGRunner.run in lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py, partition block at lines 467-497, computes succeeded_nodes, failed_nodes, skipped_nodes, and cancelled_nodes by iterating only self._results, whose entries are solely the nodes dispatched during the current invocation plus the default records added for terminal SKIPPED/CANCELLED scheduler entries. Nodes already terminal in the scheduler when run() is entered are therefore dropped from every partition: a scheduler entry in FAILED state never reaches failed_nodes, and a pre-SUCCEEDED entry never reaches succeeded_nodes. This contradicts the low/dag_engine_lite_impl.pyi GROUNDING clause for run, which directs the succeeded, failed, skipped, and cancelled tuples to be gathered from _results and _scheduler states, and the low/dag_engine_lite.pyi DAGRunReport contract, which requires the returned report to capture all node states with failed_nodes being the identifiers of all nodes that failed. The halt-on-empty-wave clause governs only when wave dispatch stops and is orthogonal to how partitions are sourced, so both obligations are simultaneously satisfiable within this file and no upstream contract decision or specification change is a prerequisite for correcting the partition derivation.
